">macOS</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • May 23, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/command-a\" target=\"_blank\">Command A+</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Cohere's open-source enterprise workhorse model released under Apache 2.0 license as a 218B sparse model for enterprise AI applications.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">open-source</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">model</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">Cohere</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • May 23, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://www.producthunt.com/products/forsy\" target=\"_blank\">Forsy</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Platform that enables users to capture and monetize their AI agent workflow data, part of the growing ecosystem around AI agents and their operational data.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"tag\">workflow</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">data</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">monetization</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Product Hunt • May 23, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n            <section class=\"whitelist-updates section\">\n                <div class=\"section-header\">Product Updates</div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub Copilot SDK GA</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">The Copilot SDK became generally available, providing developers with programmatic access to Copilot capabilities.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">SDK</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 2, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">June 2026 Copilot Wave</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Multiple Copilot updates including larger context windows with configurable reasoning levels, Chat improvements for PRs, and Enterprise Teams GA.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">context</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">enterprise</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 2, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">GPT-5.2 Models Deprecated</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">GitHub deprecated GPT-5.2 and GPT-5.2-Codex models for Copilot users as part of the June 2026 update cycle.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Deprecated</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">models</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 5, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">Fix with Copilot for Actions</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">New 'Fix with Copilot' feature for failing GitHub Actions available in Pro, Pro+, and Max tiers for AI-assisted debugging.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type feature\">Feature</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">debugging</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">CI/CD</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 4, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\">VS IDE Updates May/June</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Copilot updates for Visual Studio (May) and VS Code with Copilot Chat bringing richer context to pull requests.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"update-type release\">Release</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">VS Code</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">PRs</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">GitHub Changelog • Jun 3, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n\n            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n            <section class=\"technical-insights section\">\n                <div class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/06/08/microsofts-open-source-tools-were-hacked-to-steal-passwords-of-ai-developers/\" target=\"_blank\">Microsoft Tools Hacked</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Microsoft shut down dozens of GitHub code repositories for Azure and AI coding tools after a security breach that stole AI developers' passwords.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">TechCrunch • Jun 8, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/openai-help-lockdown-mode/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI Lockdown Mode</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">OpenAI released Lockdown Mode to help prevent data exfiltration from prompt injection attacks by limiting outbound network requests.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">prompt injection</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Simon Willison • Jun 5, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/5/ladybird-no-public-prs/\" target=\"_blank\">Ladybird No Public PRs</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Ladybird browser will no longer accept public PRs because AI-generated patches no longer indicate substantial effort or good faith.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">open source</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">AI ethics</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Simon Willison • Jun 5, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/4/ai-enthusiists-race-against-time/\" target=\"_blank\">AI Enthusiasts vs Skeptics</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Charity Majors captures the dynamic: enthusiasts see discontinuous leaps and can't afford to wait, while skeptics see reliability degrade with no natural feedback loop connecting them.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"insight-type opinion\">Opinion</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">engineering culture</span>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"source\">Simon Willison • Jun 4, 2026</div>\n                </div>\n\n                <div class=\"item\">\n                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/3/uber-caps-ai-tools/\" target=\"_blank\">Uber Caps AI Tool Costs</a>\n                    </div>\n                    <div class=\"item-description\">Uber limiting all employees to $1,500 monthly token spending per AI coding tool after reportedly blowing their 2026 AI budget in four months.</div>\n                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                        <span class=\"insight-type technical\">Technical</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">cost management</span>\n                        <span class=\"tag\">enterprise<